# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this project.

## What Was Implemented

### 1. Package Installation
- Created `package.json` with project metadata and dependencies
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version 1.6.1) using npm
- Generated `package-lock.json` for dependency locking

### 2. Analytics Integration
- Added Vercel Web Analytics to `index.html` using ES module import from jsDelivr CDN
- Used the `inject()` function from `@vercel/analytics` to initialize analytics tracking
- Placed the analytics script in the `<head>` section after Google Analytics for proper initialization order

### 3. Configuration Files
- Created `.gitignore` to exclude `node_modules/` directory from version control

## Files Created/Modified

### Created:
- `package.json` - Node.js package configuration with @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - npm lock file for consistent dependency installation
- `.gitignore` - Git ignore file to exclude node_modules

### Modified:
- `index.html` - Added Vercel Web Analytics script using ES module import

## Implementation Details

The implementation uses the CDN approach for static HTML sites:
```html
<!-- Vercel Web Analytics -->
<script type="module">
  import { inject } from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@vercel/analytics@1.6.1/dist/index.mjs';
  inject();
</script>
```

This approach:
- Loads the analytics library from jsDelivr CDN (fast, reliable, free)
- Uses ES modules for modern browser compatibility
- Calls `inject()` to automatically initialize page view tracking
- Works seamlessly with static HTML without requiring a build step

## Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Deploy this project to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
3. After deployment, analytics data will start flowing automatically
4. View analytics in your Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab

## Notes

- Analytics tracking is automatically disabled in development mode
- Only tracks page views in production when deployed to Vercel
- No personal data is collected; analytics are privacy-friendly
- The existing Google Analytics integration remains unchanged
- Both analytics solutions can coexist without conflicts
